# mono.xrs - the mono screen (stereo rung 1) reaches BOTH eyes.
#
# The gate that makes per-eye captures trustworthy (docs/VERIFICATION.md): the
# game frame on the head-locked quad must composite non-black in the left eye
# AND the right eye, with the same bounding box in both (the quad sits at the
# same place for both eyes; the eye parallax on a 1.75 m screen is under one
# percent of the eye). A black eye is attributed by the sim's own log line
# (`xrsim: eye L composited BLACK ... COMPOSITOR fault` or `... APP fault`).
#
# Run it in GAMEPLAY (boot.ps1 first): the title and the menus are mostly black
# and a load screen is legitimately so.
reset
@mod stereo mono
@frames 60
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert layersLastFrame ge 1
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot mono
@assert capNonBlackL ge 10
@assert capNonBlackR ge 10
@capassert layers.0.type eq quad
@capassert stats.nonBlackPctL ge 10
@capassert stats.nonBlackPctR ge 10
@capsame stats.bboxPctL stats.bboxPctR 2
